'''Dongfeng Motor Group Co., Ltd.''', [[doing business as]] '''DFG''', is a Chinese holding company based in [[Wuhan]], [[Hubei]]. Its [[H share]]s were listed on the [[Hong Kong stock exchange]].

Dongfeng Motor Group formed several joint ventures with other foreign automobile makers, namely [[Luxgen]], [[Honda]], [[Renault]]-[[Nissan]] and [[Stellantis]] (which was created by the merger of [[Fiat Chrysler Automobiles]] and [[Groupe PSA]]). It has also leased several trademarks from the parent company [[Dongfeng Motor Corporation]] since 2005.<ref name=DFG2016AR/>{{rp|41}}

Dongfeng Motor Group was ranked 550th in 2017 [[Forbes Global 2000|''Forbes'' Global 2000 List]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.forbes.com/companies/dongfeng-motor-group/|title=Dongfeng Motor Group on the Forbes Growth Champions List|website=forbes.com|access-date=25 April 2018|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170902114952/https://www.forbes.com/companies/dongfeng-motor-group/|archive-date=2 September 2017}}</ref> {{as of|2018|04|30}}, the market capitalization of its [[H shares]] (about 33.15% of total [[share capital]]{{Hair space}}<ref name=DFG2016AR/>{{rp|166}}) was [[Hong Kong dollar|HK$]]24.931&nbsp;[[1,000,000,000|billion]].<ref name=Hshare/>

==History==
Dongfeng Motor Group (then known as Dongfeng Motor Co., Ltd.) was incorporated on 18 May 2001 as a [[special purpose vehicle]] for [[Debt restructuring|debt-to-equity swap]] of [[Dongfeng Motor Corporation]].<ref name=prospectus>{{cite book|url=http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/SEHK/2005/1124/LTN20051124007.htm|title=Prospectus|date=24 November 2005|access-date=29 July 2017|publisher=Dongfeng Motor Group|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170729180105/http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/SEHK/2005/1124/LTN20051124007.htm|archive-date=29 July 2017}}</ref>{{rp|89}} The other shareholders were fellow state-owned financial companies [[China Huarong Asset Management]], [[China Cinda Asset Management]], [[China Orient Asset Management]], [[China Great Wall Asset Management]] and [[China Development Bank]] for a total of 42.86% stake.<ref name=prospectus/>{{rp|89}} In 2003, [new] [[Dongfeng Motor Co., Ltd.]] was incorporated as a joint venture of Dongfeng Motor Group and [[Nissan]]. Dongfeng Motor Group, at that time still known as [old] Dongfeng Motor Co., Ltd., was renamed to Dongfeng Automobile Industry Investment.<ref name=prospectus/>{{rp|89}}

In August 2004, Dongfeng Motor Group bought back all the stakes of Dongfeng Motor Group from other stakeholders, for a total of {{CNY|link=yes|4.6&nbsp;[[1,000,000,000|billion]]}}.<ref name=prospectus/>{{rp|98}} It also became a "company limited by shares" ({{zh|s=股份有限公司}}, analog of [[public limited company]]) in October 2004, with a new name Dongfeng Motor Group.<ref name=prospectus/>{{rp|99}} The company issued [[H share]] and became a listed company on 7 December 2005.<ref name=DFG2016AR>{{cite web|url=http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/SEHK/2017/0427/LTN20170427585.pdf|title=2016 Annual Report|date=27 April 2017|access-date=28 July 2017|publisher=Dongfeng Motor Group|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170728120057/http://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/SEHK/2017/0427/LTN20170427585.pdf|archive-date=28 July 2017}}</ref><ref name=Hshare>{{cite web|url=http://www.hkex.com.hk/market-data/statistics/consolidated-reports/china-dimension?sc_lang=en|title=List of H Share Companies (Main Board)|date=30 April 2018|access-date=12 May 2018|publisher=Hong Kong Stock Exchange}}</ref>

In 2014, the plan to establish Dongfeng Commercial Vehicle was approved by the [[National Development and Reform Commission]]. It would acquire some business and assets from the joint venture [[Dongfeng Motor Co., Ltd.]] In turn [[Volvo]] acquired 45% stake of Dongfeng Commercial Vehicle from Dongfeng Motor Group. At the same time [[Dongfeng Nissan Diesel Motor]] would be a wholly owned subsidiary of Dongfeng Commercial Vehicle.<ref>{{cite press release|url=http://www.ndrc.gov.cn/fzgggz/gyfz/gyfz/201401/t20140124_677234.html|title=东风汽车集团股份有限公司和沃尔沃集团重组东风商用车业务项目通过核准|date=7 January 2014|access-date=29 July 2017|publisher=National Development and Reform Commission|language=zh|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170729174106/http://www.ndrc.gov.cn/fzgggz/gyfz/gyfz/201401/t20140124_677234.html|archive-date=29 July 2017}}</ref> In January 2015, Dongfeng Commercial Vehicle was established.<ref>{{cite press release|url=http://www.dongfengtrucks.com/media/corporate-news/dongfeng-commercial-vehicles-co-ltd-joint-venture-officially-established/|title=Dongfeng Commercial Vehicles Co., Ltd. Joint Venture Officially Established|date=28 January 2015|access-date=30 July 2017|publisher=Dongfeng Motor Group|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170802155629/http://www.dongfengtrucks.com/media/corporate-news/dongfeng-commercial-vehicles-co-ltd-joint-venture-officially-established/|archive-date=2 August 2017}}</ref>

